id: zwave_nvm_restore_fix
label: Z-Wave NVM Restore Fix
package: custom
description: >
  Wraps ZPAL's zpal_nvm_backup_write, which erases the flash page after the NVM when a
  write ends exactly at the end of the NVM. Every full NVM restore over the Serial API
  ends with such a write, so it erases the manufacturing tokens and bootloader keys.
  This component writes the last word of that write itself, so the write ZPAL sees ends
  inside the last NVM page.
category: Z-Wave|Platform
quality: production
source:
  - path: src/zwave_nvm_restore_fix.c
provides:
  - name: zwave_nvm_restore_fix
requires:
  - name: nvm3_default
toolchain_settings:
  - option: gcc_linker_option
    value: "-Wl,--wrap=zpal_nvm_backup_write"
  - option: llvm_linker_option
    value: "-Wl,--wrap=zpal_nvm_backup_write"

metadata:
  nabucasa:
    wrap_definitions:
      # The stack's call to `zpal_nvm_backup_write` is inlined by LTO unless ZPAL's definition is kept out of it
      zpal_nvm_backup_write: "libzpal_EFR32ZG23-gcc.a:zpal_nvm.c.obj"
